    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367-a1">

                <pb facs="0666" n="596" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg596"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 591.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">ultimatum.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-09-23"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 23,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">President</hi>: We have the honor to announce to you
                    that if the pillage, incendiarism, and murder which are being committed since
                    yesterday in the capital by the soldiers of the Government, and particularly by
                    the mob, do not cease before night the vessels of war in the harbor will take
                    such measures as they shall judge necessary; that is to say, they will find
                    themselves under the necessity not only of sweeping the streets of the one and
                    the other, but moreover will be under the dire necessity of bombarding the forts
                    and even your palace, where sufficient troops should be found to restore the
                    necessary order and tranquillity in the capital.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item>H. T. C. HUNT,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">In charge of H. B. M.’s
                                    Legation</hi>.</item>
                            <item>C. FRENSBERG,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Consul of
                                Germany</hi>.</item>
                            <item>TH. SKEITBERG,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Vice-Consul of Greece
                                    and Consul of Belgium</hi>.</item>
                            <item>E. BURDEL,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires of
                                    France</hi>.</item>
                            <item>ANT. ARANDA,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Consul of
                                Spain</hi>.</item>
                            <item>HUGH TWEEDY,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Consul of Norway and
                                    Sweden</hi>.</item>
                            <item>HERMANN PETERS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Consul-General of the
                                    Netherlands.</hi></item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
